WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:03.730
The inter-school tournament ended in a draw.

00:03.730 --> 00:07.900
The city of Nankatsu has decided to enter the upcoming Nationals

00:07.900 --> 00:10.860
with a city selection team, Nankatsu FC.

00:10.860 --> 00:12.740
Aiming to become regular members,

00:12.740 --> 00:14.410
Tsubasa, Misaki and Ishizaki

00:14.410 --> 00:17.580
have been hard at practice.

00:17.580 --> 00:19.910
Meanwhile, Roberto asked Tsubasa's parents to entrust

00:19.910 --> 00:22.290
Tsubasa to him and let Tsubasa attend a

00:23.040 --> 00:26.460
football institute in Brazil.

00:27.080 --> 00:29.670
Tsubasa's heart wavers.

00:29.670 --> 00:32.380
In the end, he decides to go to Brazil.

00:32.920 --> 00:35.550
Chosen as a member of Nankatsu FC,

00:35.550 --> 00:38.140
he moves onward to the preliminaries of the national tournament!

00:52.110 --> 00:57.740
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

00:52.110 --> 00:57.740
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

00:57.740 --> 01:02.750
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

00:57.740 --> 01:02.750
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:03.410 --> 01:08.580
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:03.410 --> 01:08.580
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:09.290 --> 01:16.930
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:09.290 --> 01:16.930
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:16.930 --> 01:22.680
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:16.930 --> 01:22.680
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:22.680 --> 01:31.190
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:22.680 --> 01:31.190
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:31.190 --> 01:36.990
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:31.190 --> 01:36.990
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:36.990 --> 01:42.910
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:36.990 --> 01:42.910
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:42.910 --> 01:44.410
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:44.410 --> 01:51.710
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:44.410 --> 01:51.710
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

01:51.710 --> 01:54.630
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

01:51.710 --> 01:54.630
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

01:54.630 --> 01:59.550
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

01:54.630 --> 01:59.550
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:10.020 --> 02:13.070
<b><b>EPISODE 10 :
KOJIRO ARRIVES</b></b>

02:12.610 --> 02:13.820
I'm counting on you!

02:13.820 --> 02:14.530
Stop him!

02:14.530 --> 02:16.940
It's okay if you can just keep Hyuga from dribbling!

02:16.940 --> 02:17.990
Okay!

02:20.740 --> 02:23.950
Do you seriously think your weak defense can stop me?!

02:23.950 --> 02:25.830
If you really want to stop me,

02:25.830 --> 02:27.540
you'd better put your life on the line!

02:27.540 --> 02:30.210
I won't let you keep the ball anymore!

02:31.540 --> 02:32.460
How's this?!

02:33.340 --> 02:35.550
Eat this shot!

02:39.970 --> 02:42.720
Kojiro Hyuga, you are the worst!

02:42.720 --> 02:43.930
You went overboard.

02:43.930 --> 02:46.680
How many more people do you intend to injure?

02:46.680 --> 02:47.850
Shut up!

02:47.850 --> 02:51.020
If these kinds of injuries scare you, you might as well quit football!

02:51.020 --> 02:52.360
This guy...

02:52.360 --> 02:56.030
Listen, this is just a practice match before the prefectural tournament.

02:56.030 --> 02:58.860
We can't afford to take these many injuries.

02:58.860 --> 03:00.780
We're ending the match here.

03:03.530 --> 03:05.790
Captain!

03:05.790 --> 03:07.870
You went a little overboard today, don't you think?

03:07.870 --> 03:09.250
What?

03:09.250 --> 03:11.540
So even you're criticizing me, huh?

03:15.130 --> 03:16.420
Have it your way, then.

03:16.420 --> 03:20.010
Go and win the preliminaries with your own football.

03:20.010 --> 03:21.010
Eh?!

03:21.010 --> 03:23.970
I won't be participating in the preliminary matches.

03:23.970 --> 03:26.560
Let's see if you can make it to the national tournament

03:26.560 --> 03:28.470
with your own skills.

03:28.470 --> 03:29.520
Captain...

03:29.520 --> 03:35.230
We will see if the way that I, Kojiro Hyuga, play,

03:35.230 --> 03:37.690
is the correct way to play, after all.

03:41.570 --> 03:42.320
Tsubasa!

03:45.370 --> 03:47.030
Nice shot, Tsubasa!

03:47.030 --> 03:49.250
Misaki's next, right?

03:53.370 --> 03:55.460
I wonder if this will really be okay...

03:59.460 --> 04:02.130
Captain Ozora leaves port in two weeks.

04:02.130 --> 04:05.220
Taking Tsubasa to Brazil on top of that...

04:05.220 --> 04:08.310
We'll be leaving Mrs. Ozora all alone.

04:08.310 --> 04:12.180
Also... Tsubasa was so ready to say he'd go to Brazil,

04:12.180 --> 04:14.020
but don't you think he'll start being lonely once he

04:14.020 --> 04:15.480
starts living by himself?

04:15.480 --> 04:17.230
Roberto!

04:18.190 --> 04:19.230
What happened?

04:19.230 --> 04:20.440
You're spacing out.

04:21.650 --> 04:24.110
Sorry. Shall we take a break?

04:24.110 --> 04:25.200
Okay.

04:25.200 --> 04:26.450
What about Ishizaki?

04:29.330 --> 04:30.700
Come on, what happened?

04:30.700 --> 04:32.290
We're only starting now.

04:35.500 --> 04:37.130
Hey, what's wrong?

04:37.130 --> 04:39.210
Your legs were getting all tangled up there in the last one...

04:39.210 --> 04:42.590
Aren't you being a little harsh!?

04:42.590 --> 04:45.010
Just give me a quick 5 minutes, let me catch my breath...

04:45.010 --> 04:48.350
Sure, it's okay for today, but there will be no breaks tomorrow!

04:48.350 --> 04:49.930
Manabu, are you some sort of demon?

04:49.930 --> 04:52.560
Listen; you, Tsubasa and Misaki

04:52.560 --> 04:55.600
were chosen as one of the 30 players for the selection team in the end.

04:55.600 --> 04:58.560
Don't you want to be among the final 15 players?

04:58.560 --> 05:01.820
Yeah. Tsubasa and Misaki will make it in for sure...

05:01.820 --> 05:03.740
But we can't be so sure about Ishizaki, right?

05:03.740 --> 05:05.820
You really don't hold back...

05:05.820 --> 05:09.370
Anyway! This is our way of cheering for you.

05:09.370 --> 05:12.580
You can't go to the nationals if you don't work hard!

05:14.250 --> 05:15.330
Got it.

05:18.080 --> 05:20.880
It'd be nice if all three of us could make it.

05:20.880 --> 05:21.880
Yeah.

05:22.760 --> 05:24.010
Here he goes again!

05:24.010 --> 05:26.550
Defense! Stop him this time!

05:34.310 --> 05:35.600
I did it!

05:35.600 --> 05:36.810
You're in top form today.

05:36.810 --> 05:40.730
This practice match doesn't even count as

05:40.730 --> 05:42.820
a warm-up for the Nankatsu FC players.

05:44.320 --> 05:45.990
He got through him!

05:45.990 --> 05:46.570
Captain!

05:47.030 --> 05:48.070
Tsubasa...

05:48.070 --> 05:50.830
This time I'll team up with you, and I'll take the championship twice in a row.

05:51.240 --> 05:52.080
Go!

05:52.080 --> 05:52.830
All right!

05:55.000 --> 05:55.870
It's useless.

05:55.870 --> 05:57.750
We can't beat Wakabayashi.

06:02.960 --> 06:04.260
End of the match!

06:04.260 --> 06:05.840
Ah, hell, I'm sorry...

06:12.760 --> 06:16.430
Hey, isn't Nankatsu FC the best?

06:16.430 --> 06:19.190
If you get the guys from Shutetsu, Tsubasa and Misaki,

06:19.190 --> 06:21.270
don't you think they can win the national championship?

06:21.270 --> 06:23.900
Yeah, I really see what you mean.

06:23.900 --> 06:26.030
Well, you can't be too sure.

06:26.030 --> 06:29.070
The national level is steadily rising.

06:29.070 --> 06:32.910
Oh yeah, you've transferred between many different schools, right?

06:32.910 --> 06:35.910
Let's take Shiba's Kujiukuri FC, for instance.

06:35.910 --> 06:38.540
They practice on the beach everyday

06:38.540 --> 06:40.500
and train their legs and lower body.

06:40.500 --> 06:42.590
That's why they never lose when it comes to running

06:42.590 --> 06:44.670
and they're also known for their persistence.

06:45.210 --> 06:48.970
The members of Osaka's Naniwa FC are tall,

06:48.970 --> 06:51.680
so they have a lot of confidence in mid-air battles.

06:51.680 --> 06:56.470
Fukuoka's Hakata FC has many team levels, ranging from adults to kids.

06:56.470 --> 06:58.180
Since they practice with many older players,

06:58.180 --> 07:00.850
they often can put even adults to shame.

07:00.850 --> 07:04.020
Wow, there really are a lot of different teams!

07:04.020 --> 07:06.980
But if we go the national tournament,

07:06.980 --> 07:10.490
the most powerful one is probably Meiwa FC.

07:10.910 --> 07:14.370
Their ace striker, Kojiro Hyuga is

07:14.370 --> 07:17.330
as skilled as Tsubasa.

07:17.330 --> 07:18.330
Are you serious?

07:18.330 --> 07:19.660
You're lying!

07:19.660 --> 07:22.000
Tsubasa managed to score a goal all by himself

07:22.000 --> 07:24.420
against the national tournament champion, Wakabayashi.

07:24.420 --> 07:26.340
All you need to know is that

07:26.340 --> 07:31.180
Kojiro is a completely different type of striker than Tsubasa.

07:31.590 --> 07:35.140
Meiwa FC... Kojiro Hyuga...

07:42.940 --> 07:45.440
I can't take this anymore.

07:49.400 --> 07:51.240
Wakabayashi!

07:51.240 --> 07:52.990
Are you going back home now, too?

07:53.910 --> 07:58.330
Ishizaki, why is it that only your clothes are dirty?

07:58.330 --> 07:59.290
Shut up!

07:59.290 --> 08:00.710
I've been doing special training

08:00.710 --> 08:02.290
to get into the final 15 of the selection team.

08:02.290 --> 08:04.630
I think all that hard work's going to be in vain, though.

08:04.630 --> 08:06.340
Damn, what's your problem?

08:09.460 --> 08:10.590
What's wrong?

08:12.170 --> 08:13.930
Nothing.

08:20.520 --> 08:23.890
I really want to meet Meiwa FC's Hyuga.

08:23.890 --> 08:26.770
He said he was different from you.

08:26.770 --> 08:28.940
Still, there's only one of you, Tsubasa.

08:28.940 --> 08:30.990
You're different from all the players in the world.

08:30.990 --> 08:31.650
That's right.

08:32.950 --> 08:35.990
There are all sorts of players in Brazil too, right?

08:35.990 --> 08:37.700
Promise me that when you go to Brazil,

08:37.700 --> 08:40.620
you won't come to back to Japan until you're a pro, Tsubasa.

08:40.620 --> 08:41.540
Yes!

08:41.540 --> 08:44.920
Still, I really want to become a pro as soon as I can!

08:44.920 --> 08:48.250
If I do that, I'll be able to play football all day long.

08:48.250 --> 08:49.340
Not so fast!

08:49.340 --> 08:51.840
If you can't win the national tournament,

08:51.840 --> 08:53.300
then you're not coming with me!

08:53.300 --> 08:55.590
That's the promise you made, Tsubasa!

08:55.590 --> 08:56.930
Of course!

08:58.350 --> 09:00.770
Being a pro is hard.

09:04.690 --> 09:05.230
Watch this.

09:11.860 --> 09:14.360
With training, your legs will eventually be strong enough for this.

09:16.110 --> 09:19.410
For now, it's still too early for you to do this.

09:19.410 --> 09:22.120
As a child whose bones are still developing, if you tried this,

09:22.120 --> 09:24.160
you would just hurt your precious legs.

09:24.160 --> 09:25.870
Okay, got it.

09:25.870 --> 09:28.830
About Wakabayashi today...

09:28.830 --> 09:30.670
It kind of looked like he was

09:30.670 --> 09:32.340
going easy on one of his legs while walking today.

09:32.340 --> 09:33.550
Eh?

09:35.630 --> 09:37.970
Finally, the day of the first practice of

09:37.970 --> 09:40.260
Nankatsu Youth Football Club has come!

09:41.010 --> 09:45.180
The initial 30 names will be narrowed down to choose

09:45.180 --> 09:49.900
15 representatives for the national tournament.

09:49.900 --> 09:50.900
All right!

09:50.900 --> 09:52.900
We'll have a match between two groups now.

09:52.900 --> 09:55.650
We have many players from Shutetsu,

09:55.650 --> 10:00.530
so we'll have a team with players from Shutetsu Elementary.

10:00.530 --> 10:02.910
The rest will make up the mixed team as I decided.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.330
We're up against Shutetsu, huh?

10:05.330 --> 10:07.370
It's our second showdown since the inter-school tournament.

10:07.370 --> 10:08.500
All right!

10:08.500 --> 10:10.630
Let's win this match, and aim to get

10:10.630 --> 10:12.920
everyone from Shutetsu in the final 15 representatives!

10:12.920 --> 10:13.750
Yeah!

10:19.970 --> 10:22.470
The match starts now.

10:28.190 --> 10:29.060
Let's see, now...

10:29.690 --> 10:32.570
Should I start this game too?

10:32.570 --> 10:35.070
We're coming at you, mixed team!

10:35.070 --> 10:36.360
Like we'd lose!

10:36.360 --> 10:38.860
Being part of the final 15 is at stake for us as well!

10:38.860 --> 10:42.490
Pass! Pass the ball around and break their rhythm.

10:42.490 --> 10:44.580
Are you Wakabayashi?

10:46.200 --> 10:47.960
Who the hell are you?

10:47.960 --> 10:52.590
Kojiro Hyuga, from Meiwa FC!

10:52.590 --> 10:55.090
Kojiro Hyuga?

10:55.090 --> 10:57.260
I'm challenging you, Wakabayashi!

10:57.260 --> 10:58.090
What?

11:01.930 --> 11:03.890
Coach, look at that!

11:05.100 --> 11:05.770
Kisugi!

11:05.770 --> 11:07.220
Okay, got it!

11:07.220 --> 11:07.850
Damn it!

11:07.850 --> 11:09.520
Shutetsu will score the first goal.

11:11.190 --> 11:12.310
What?

11:14.650 --> 11:16.570
Let's go, Shutetsu.

11:18.190 --> 11:19.820
Genzo Wakabayashi!

11:19.820 --> 11:20.990
Kojiro!

11:20.990 --> 11:21.610
Eh?!

11:21.610 --> 11:22.820
What did you say, Misaki?

11:22.820 --> 11:25.160
Then, is he the guy from Meiwa FC?

11:25.160 --> 11:26.580
Captain, this...

11:26.580 --> 11:27.410
It's okay.

11:27.410 --> 11:29.620
I'll accept his challenge.

11:29.620 --> 11:32.330
Coach, is this all right?

11:33.960 --> 11:37.090
So that's Kojiro Hyuga...

11:37.840 --> 11:39.220
This bastard...

11:39.220 --> 11:42.180
How dare you get in the way of my chance to score?

11:43.090 --> 11:44.720
Get out of my way!

11:44.720 --> 11:46.140
Are you screwing with us?

11:46.140 --> 11:47.970
Shutetsu! We'll all go and stop him!

11:53.350 --> 11:56.020
He's running straight at the goal with no hesitation!

11:56.020 --> 11:58.530
He's just blowing past them in a straight line!

11:58.530 --> 12:01.490
You're right. While your style as a striker has finesse, Tsubasa,

12:01.490 --> 12:03.360
he plays with sheer force.

12:03.360 --> 12:05.320
What are you doing, Shutetsu?

12:05.320 --> 12:07.370
Hurry up and steal the ball from him!

12:07.370 --> 12:08.790
Go, Takasugi!

12:08.790 --> 12:11.160
You won't be blown away in a one-on-one confrontation.

12:11.160 --> 12:11.870
Yes.

12:17.960 --> 12:19.260
You bastard!

12:19.260 --> 12:20.590
You hit him on purpose!

12:20.590 --> 12:21.800
Shut it!

12:21.800 --> 12:25.050
My football is different from your soft football.

12:26.430 --> 12:28.350
Let's do this, Wakabayashi.

12:28.350 --> 12:32.980
Show me the skills of a genius goalkeeper!

12:34.190 --> 12:36.310
Wakabayashi, stop him!

12:53.330 --> 12:56.920
So this is the extent of the so-called genius goalkeeper Wakabayashi's skill?

12:56.920 --> 13:00.340
He couldn't even move a muscle against my shot.

13:02.630 --> 13:03.970
Misaki.

13:03.970 --> 13:06.840
It's better to not show him your power now, Tsubasa.

13:10.470 --> 13:11.430
Misaki?

13:11.430 --> 13:12.890
Kojiro.

13:12.890 --> 13:15.140
So it's you, Misaki.

13:15.140 --> 13:18.940
What, so you've moved here this time?

13:18.940 --> 13:22.820
If you are a member of this team, then I'll tell you, too.

13:22.820 --> 13:24.950
The champion of this year's national tournament

13:25.450 --> 13:27.950
will be Meiwa FC.

13:27.950 --> 13:30.080
See you!

13:30.910 --> 13:34.790
Kojiro, if you came here to sniff around,

13:34.790 --> 13:36.830
you missed one thing.

13:37.580 --> 13:40.920
This team has a boy named Tsubasa Ozora.

13:40.920 --> 13:43.630
You went back without getting to know him.

13:44.300 --> 13:45.470
Captain...

13:52.180 --> 13:54.100
I can't believe it.

13:54.100 --> 13:57.770
How can Wakabayashi lose to someone other than Tsubasa?

13:57.770 --> 14:00.360
He went back home after that...

14:00.700 --> 14:02.110
Oh!

14:02.110 --> 14:04.820
SIGN: NAKAI ORTHOPEDICS

14:05.320 --> 14:06.110
Wakabayashi!

14:17.790 --> 14:19.960
Well, you sure found me at a bad time.

14:20.380 --> 14:22.880
Did you really hurt your leg?

14:22.880 --> 14:26.130
So that's why you didn't react to that shoot.

14:26.130 --> 14:29.050
No. Even if I had reacted,

14:29.050 --> 14:30.720
I'm not sure I could've caught it.

14:30.720 --> 14:34.640
It really was a powerful shot.

14:35.430 --> 14:39.350
Besides, I don't want to make excuses for losing.

14:39.350 --> 14:41.400
My injury is my own fault.

14:41.860 --> 14:45.440
Tsubasa, we'll definitely go to the nationals.

14:45.440 --> 14:47.990
I know Kojiro Hyuga will be there, too.

14:47.990 --> 14:50.160
We'll pay him him back for this.

14:51.200 --> 14:52.660
Yeah.

15:10.590 --> 15:12.090
Good morning, Kojiro.

15:12.090 --> 15:15.060
Morning. Aren't you going to work early, mom?

15:15.060 --> 15:17.480
Listen, don't you worry about me.

15:17.480 --> 15:20.310
Go and play the football you love.

15:21.100 --> 15:23.560
I'm doing this for football.

15:25.070 --> 15:29.530
Mom has worked a lot of jobs since dad's gone,

15:29.530 --> 15:32.570
and I can't be the only one here who gets to only do what they love.

15:33.240 --> 15:36.330
Good morning. I'm here to help.

15:36.330 --> 15:38.790
Thanks for helping me all the time. This really saves me a lot of trouble.

15:38.790 --> 15:40.830
It's all a part of my training.

15:42.710 --> 15:45.670
When I start middle school,

15:45.670 --> 15:48.090
I'll need more money.

15:48.090 --> 15:51.260
Plus, there are three little kids after me.

15:51.260 --> 15:54.140
My brothers and sisters.

15:54.140 --> 15:56.140
Take it. It's today's gift for you.

15:56.140 --> 15:57.930
Thank you very much!

15:58.520 --> 16:01.600
I'll change this daily life with football!

16:01.600 --> 16:03.940
I won't let anyone in my family suffer!

16:03.940 --> 16:07.530
For that, I have to improve my football

16:07.530 --> 16:09.690
and participate in big tournaments as much as possible.

16:10.360 --> 16:14.700
I will make sure I get into the national tournament too!

16:18.700 --> 16:20.660
Good morning, brother.

16:20.660 --> 16:22.830
Oh! You guys are awake.

16:22.830 --> 16:24.880
Mom's gone?

16:24.880 --> 16:27.960
Yeah. I'll make you a quick breakfast.

16:31.550 --> 16:33.840
Your dad will be leaving on another voyage, today.

16:33.840 --> 16:36.600
Since you decided to go to Brazil,

16:36.600 --> 16:41.020
you probably won't be here when I come back next time.

16:41.020 --> 16:41.850
Yeah.

16:41.850 --> 16:46.520
Captain, Tsubasa made me a promise regarding that.

16:46.520 --> 16:47.820
A promise?

16:47.820 --> 16:50.320
Unless he wins the national tournament,

16:50.320 --> 16:52.700
he won't be coming to Brazil.

16:52.700 --> 16:54.860
That's hard...

16:54.860 --> 17:00.040
But ultimately, pointless. Tsubasa can definitely win Nationals.

17:00.040 --> 17:01.750
Thanks, dad.

17:01.750 --> 17:05.250
Then Tsubasa, make a promise with your dad too.

17:05.250 --> 17:06.630
What?

17:06.630 --> 17:09.590
If you get a hat-trick in today's match,

17:09.590 --> 17:12.130
I'll let you go to Brazil.

17:12.130 --> 17:15.590
You know, you were the one saying to let him go...!

17:15.590 --> 17:19.010
I want to see how serious Tsubasa is about going.

17:19.010 --> 17:22.770
Sure thing! I just have to do a hat-trick today, right?

17:23.140 --> 17:26.020
Then I'll need to record it perfectly!

17:26.560 --> 17:28.400
This is going to be Tsubasa's last

17:28.400 --> 17:30.940
tournament in Japan, right?

17:32.780 --> 17:33.860
Captain!

17:35.110 --> 17:36.200
Hyuga!

17:36.200 --> 17:37.450
Please wait!

17:37.450 --> 17:38.740
Are you seriously not going to enter

17:38.740 --> 17:40.120
the prefectural tournament?

17:40.120 --> 17:43.500
I thought you guys were going to get to Nationals

17:43.500 --> 17:45.040
with your football?

17:46.120 --> 17:48.880
See you later. I'll be waiting for the good news.

17:48.880 --> 17:51.050
Make sure you guys win.

17:52.710 --> 17:55.050
He doesn't have to be so adamant.

17:55.050 --> 17:58.180
No. We relied on him too much.

17:58.180 --> 18:02.310
And he has a reason to win, no matter what.

18:02.310 --> 18:02.970
Reason?

18:03.390 --> 18:07.100
Last year, his family lost their father.

18:08.400 --> 18:10.560
He has many young siblings, and his

18:10.560 --> 18:13.070
mother works in several different jobs.

18:13.070 --> 18:16.610
In her stead, he takes care of everything in his house.

18:17.110 --> 18:19.990
That's why he wants to win the nationals,

18:19.990 --> 18:21.910
so a pro team will scout him.

18:21.910 --> 18:25.290
That way he can help his mother get by easier.

18:25.290 --> 18:29.790
Oh, right. There'll be a lot of scouts coming to the Nationals.

18:29.790 --> 18:30.750
Okay, then.

18:30.750 --> 18:34.130
We must do our best. For our captain, too!

18:34.130 --> 18:35.510
Yeah!

18:36.970 --> 18:39.970
All over the country, the preliminaries for

18:39.970 --> 18:42.100
the National Tournament have started.

18:43.560 --> 18:45.100
I got selected again!

18:45.680 --> 18:48.020
Wakabayashi, it's about to start.

18:48.020 --> 18:49.900
Yeah. It's starting.

18:49.900 --> 18:51.110
Is your leg okay?

18:51.110 --> 18:54.110
I mean, that's why I'm here.

18:54.480 --> 18:57.240
The third match in the first round will be starting now.

18:57.650 --> 19:01.740
Nankatsu FC will be going up against Fuji FC.

19:02.070 --> 19:05.080
It's your first match. Give it all you've got!

19:05.080 --> 19:06.000
Yes, sir!

19:07.750 --> 19:10.370
So, I'm on the bench?

19:11.670 --> 19:14.840
Tsubasa, I'm here to cheer you on.

19:14.840 --> 19:16.010
Dad!

19:16.010 --> 19:18.260
Score that hat-trick!

19:18.590 --> 19:19.510
Yes!

19:22.390 --> 19:26.060
Go, Tsubasa!

19:26.680 --> 19:29.390
The match starts with a Nankatsu kick-off!

19:30.640 --> 19:32.650
Just wait, Nationals.

19:32.650 --> 19:35.650
I'll be able to show everyone my skill.

19:35.650 --> 19:37.900
If I do that, I can probably get a football scholarship

19:37.900 --> 19:39.320
an a football-focused secondary school.

19:39.320 --> 19:42.910
Then I'll be able to fully devote myself to playing football.

19:43.570 --> 19:47.080
It's in! Nankatsu scores an early lead with a goal!

19:47.080 --> 19:48.830
That's one.

19:48.830 --> 19:50.000
Yes!

19:50.870 --> 19:54.750
That's right. Only you can carve your own path.

19:57.960 --> 19:59.720
Nankatsu scores a second goal!

20:06.060 --> 20:08.680
This time, Tsubasa dribbled in by himself and took the shot!

20:09.140 --> 20:11.440
I was worrying about my leg...

20:11.440 --> 20:14.310
But if this is how it'll be, I can rest easy.

20:14.310 --> 20:14.690
Do your best—

20:14.690 --> 20:16.610
Go, Tsubasa!

20:16.610 --> 20:18.320
Keep it up!

20:18.320 --> 20:19.820
Mark him! Get to him!

20:26.370 --> 20:29.870
Tsubasa and Misaki play an excellent one-two pass!

20:29.870 --> 20:32.370
Here goes their combination play!

20:32.370 --> 20:35.790
He runs and fires off a volley!

20:37.130 --> 20:39.090
The keeper can't react!

20:39.090 --> 20:42.630
Tsubasa has scored a hat-trick early in the first half!

20:42.630 --> 20:44.510
I did it, dad!

20:44.510 --> 20:48.970
Good! Dad is going to off on a voyage to sea on his favorite ship,

20:48.970 --> 20:54.520
so win the Nationals, and go to Brazil and develop your football!

20:54.520 --> 20:57.520
Yeah! Take care, dad!

20:59.650 --> 21:00.860
Take care!

21:00.860 --> 21:02.900
Yeah. I'll be back.

21:04.660 --> 21:08.740
<b>NANKATSU SC 7 - 0 FUJI FC
QUALIFIES FOR THE SECOND TOUR</b>

21:10.750 --> 21:14.620
There! It's time for the kids to go to sleep.

21:15.040 --> 21:16.880
Oh! Welcome back, mom.

21:17.250 --> 21:19.460
I've made dinner.

21:19.460 --> 21:20.550
Did you win?

21:20.550 --> 21:22.550
Didn't you have a match today?

21:22.550 --> 21:24.880
Yeah. Those guys would've won.

21:24.880 --> 21:27.090
Is it okay to not play?

21:29.510 --> 21:33.520
Nankatsu has steadily advanced through the bracket

21:33.520 --> 21:36.040
after winning the first round.

21:36.040 --> 21:37.560
Meanwhile...

21:38.310 --> 21:40.320
It's in! 2-0!

21:40.320 --> 21:42.940
In this match to decide the representative team for Saitama,

21:42.940 --> 21:47.070
Nanbu FC has pulled a two goal lead over Meiwa FC early in the first half!

21:47.450 --> 21:48.870
We can't do this.

21:48.870 --> 21:52.120
We barely won the quarter-finals ourselves yesterday, but—

21:52.120 --> 21:55.080
Without Hyuga, we're—

21:59.540 --> 22:01.420
Captain.

22:08.140 --> 22:10.640
Looks like it's our turn.

22:10.640 --> 22:12.060
Let's go, Takeshi!

22:12.060 --> 22:13.810
Yes, captain!

22:38.960 --> 22:44.840
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.960 --> 22:44.840
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.850
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.850
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.850 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.850 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:02.310
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:02.310
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.270 --> 23:08.450
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.270 --> 23:08.450
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.360 --> 23:15.160
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.360 --> 23:15.160
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.160 --> 23:21.210
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.210 --> 23:26.210
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.210 --> 23:26.210
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.510 --> 23:33.390
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.510 --> 23:33.390
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.390 --> 23:39.270
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.270 --> 23:46.150
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.270 --> 23:46.150
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.240 --> 24:00.250
COMING UP, EPISODE 11 : A SURPRISINGLY DIFFICULT MATCH
